<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Token-Factored Architecture and Frozen Token Stream Variant</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix specifies the architecture used throughout the paper to avoid confusion with additive disentanglement methods (e.g., DeBERTa). Our design is an <em id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">architectural</em> separation of streams, not a decomposition inside attention. The separation is enforced by where updates are written, not by extra attention terms.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Stream Factorization</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each layer maintains two streams:</p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E10X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=X_{T}^{(l)}+X_{E}^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=X_{T}^{(l)}+X_{E}^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E10Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{T}^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{T}^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{TokenEmbedding}(\text{input\_ids})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>TokenEmbedding</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>input_ids</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{TokenEmbedding}(\text{input\_ids})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E10Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{E}^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{E}^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is the token stream (interpretable, token-linked), while <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{E}</annotation></semantics></math> is the embedding-like stream (contextual, abductive). The key architectural constraint is that attention updates <em id="A1.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">only</em> <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the FFN updates <em id="A1.SS1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">only</em> <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{E}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Factored Self-Attention (LFA/CFM)</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{CLN}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>CLN</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{CLN}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> denote channel-wise layer normalization applied independently per head. Queries and keys observe both streams, but values are computed only from <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{\text{attn}}^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mtext>attn</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{\text{attn}}^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{CLN}(X_{T}^{(l-1)}+X_{E}^{(l-1)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>CLN</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{CLN}(X_{T}^{(l-1)}+X_{E}^{(l-1)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=X_{\text{attn}}^{(l)}W_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mtext>attn</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=X_{\text{attn}}^{(l)}W_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle K^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle K^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=X_{\text{attn}}^{(l)}W_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mtext>attn</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=X_{\text{attn}}^{(l)}W_{K}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=X_{T}^{(l-1)}\tilde{W}_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=X_{T}^{(l-1)}\tilde{W}_{V}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{T}^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{T}^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=X_{T}^{(l-1)}+\text{Attention}(Q^{(l)},K^{(l)},V^{(l)})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>Attention</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=X_{T}^{(l-1)}+\text{Attention}(Q^{(l)},K^{(l)},V^{(l)}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">To preserve channelization, the value and output projections must respect head structure. In the token-factored case we use Kronecker-lifted mixing,
<math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{W}_{V}=W_{\text{head}}\otimes I_{d_{head}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mtext>head</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{W}_{V}=W_{\text{head}}\otimes I_{d_{head}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{W}_{O}=W^{\prime}_{\text{head}}\otimes I_{d_{head}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>O</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mtext>head</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{W}_{O}=W^{\prime}_{\text{head}}\otimes I_{d_{head}}</annotation></semantics></math>, so each head remains a structured channel. This ensures attention performs symbolic routing over token-linked representations while keeping contextual updates separate.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>FFN Update (Observes Both Streams, Maintains Separation)</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The FFN consumes the combined state but writes only to <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{E}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{\text{ffn}}^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mtext>ffn</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{\text{ffn}}^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{CLN}(X_{T}^{(l)}+X_{E}^{(l-1)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>CLN</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{CLN}(X_{T}^{(l)}+X_{E}^{(l-1)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{E}^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{E}^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=X_{E}^{(l-1)}+\text{FFN}(X_{\text{ffn}}^{(l)})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>FFN</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mtext>ffn</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=X_{E}^{(l-1)}+\text{FFN}(X_{\text{ffn}}^{(l)}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Critically, while FFN observes both streams, it writes only to <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{E}</annotation></semantics></math>, maintaining
architectural separation. Attention routes token-linked information while the
FFN integrates semantics into the embedding-like stream, but the streams remain
distinct—fusion occurs only at the output layer (lm_head).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Frozen Token Stream Variant</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The frozen token stream variant fixes the token-like stream to the input while still training all parameters end-to-end. In FTS, the attention path uses raw token-stream values and an identity output projection (<math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{W}_{V}=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{W}_{V}=I</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{W}_{O}=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>O</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{W}_{O}=I</annotation></semantics></math>), preserving channelization by construction. This stream update mode is shared by D-Cas, LFA, and CFM; the models differ only in their mixing constraints (dense vs. independent attention/FFN):</p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{T}^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{T}^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
